  "solution": {
    "text": "Sucralose is an artificial sweetener. The majority of ingested sucralose is not broken down by the body, so it is no caloric. The structure of the Sucralose is<br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/482cf66b-b26c-4570-a689-e48f800baf6b-image.png\" style=\"width: 230px; height: 145px;\" /><br /><br />Alitame is an aspartic acid-containing dipeptide sweetener. The structure of Alitame is<br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/22b33053-f241-4708-92a9-94c84d2f6d30-image.png\" style=\"width: 230px; height: 97px;\" /><br /><br />Saccharin is an artificial sweetener with effectively no food energy which is about 400 times as sweet as sucrose or table sugar, but has a bitter or metallic aftertaste, especially at high concentrations. It is used to sweeten products such as drinks, candies, cookies, medicines, and toothpaste. The structure of the Saccharin is<br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e5d2b958-2f23-4a3b-ad0b-6fc525e2258b-image.png\" style=\"width: 140px; height: 134px;\" /><br /><br />Aspartame is an artificial, non-saccharide sweetener used as a sugar substitute in some foods and beverages. The structure of Aspartame is<br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/2d862643-4df4-4c75-938c-cb0b0cc959b3-image.png\" style=\"width: 220px; height: 133px;\" />",
